  "applicability_scope": [
    "Level 1 review by Shuangping Li on 13 November 2026 of twelve P27 Results/Overview.lean statements against the ICML 2026 OpenReview PDF, with AI-assisted statement translations.",
    "Theorems 3.1 and 3.4: element-valued mistake-feedback generation and set-valued one-query-per-round generation are each equivalent to a countable inner cover, over a countable infinite universe and classes of infinite languages.",
    "Theorem 3.2: set- and element-valued mistake feedback are equivalent; the set-valued feedback bit judges the first output element in one fixed injection of the universe into Nat.",
    "Theorem 3.3: some class over Nat is generatable with query feedback by an element-valued but not by any set-valued generator.",
    "Corollaries 3.6 and 3.7: countable-union closure, and zero-example generation with the source's literal success condition z_n in K.",
    "Corollary 3.8: eventually correct mistake and query feedback are characterized by countable inner covers, with success required on every sample stream.",
    "Theorem 3.9, set-to-element direction, and the Appendix Lemma A.8 counterexample (a fresh successful generator for a one-language class with no self-locking prefix along one presentation).",
    "Theorem 3.10 components A.9 (finite inner cover suffices), A.12, and A.13.",
    "Recursive project-local statement-relevant definitions, including the inner covers, the mistake, query, zero-example, and eventually correct interaction models and their feedback runs, the canonical-order first element, and the no-feedback element and set generation predicates."
  ],
  "not_automatically_tracked": [
    "theorem_3_9_of_selfLocking: its premise (Lemma A.8 for every successful generator) fails even for a one-language class, so it is not evidence for the element-to-set direction of Theorem 3.9.",
